# Cursor Rules for Next.js + Supabase + Tailwind + Radix UI
# Author: Ajay Prompt

project:
  name: Next.js Web App
  description: >
    A scalable, adaptive, and responsive web application built using Next.js, Supabase, TailwindCSS, and Radix UI.
    Follows modern Next.js standards for routing, layouts, and server components.

stack:
  framework: Next.js 14+
  backend: Supabase
  ui: TailwindCSS, Radix UI
  language: TypeScript
  router: App Router (pages/layouts as per Next.js docs)
  style_system: Tailwind + Component Modules

rules:
  - Always use TypeScript (.tsx, .ts).
  - Use Next.js App Router (`app/` directory) for routing and layouts.
  - Follow atomic file structure and modular imports.
  - All components must be functional React components.
  - Use Server Components by default; only use Client Components when interaction or state is required (`"use client"`).
  - Pages must be a Server Side! create a component if needs to used the "use client"
  - Use async/await for all Supabase data operations.
  - Maintain separation of concerns:
      * `/app` → routing, layouts, pages
      * `/components` → UI and reusable components
      * `/lib` → utilities, Supabase client, helper functions
      * `/styles` → Tailwind configuration and globals
      * `/hooks` → custom React hooks
      * `/types` → TypeScript interfaces and types
      * `/context` → React context providers (if needed)
  - Manage Supabase client via `/lib/supabaseClient.ts`.
  - Handle all environment variables securely via `.env.local` with `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix for client access.
  - Always validate Supabase data responses and handle errors gracefully.
  - For UI:
      * Use Tailwind for layout and spacing.
      * Use Radix UI primitives for accessibility and interactivity.
      * Keep design adaptive and mobile-first.
      * Avoid inline styles unless dynamic.
  - Keep components small and single-responsibility.
  - Reuse layouts where possible using `layout.tsx` files.
  - Avoid prop drilling by using Context or hooks where necessary.
  - Always ensure accessibility (aria labels, keyboard navigation).
  - Add comments for non-trivial logic.
  - Prefer Next.js `Image` and `Link` components for optimization.

standards:
  naming:
    - Folders and files: kebab-case (e.g. `user-profile`, `auth-layout`)
    - Components and hooks: PascalCase (e.g. `UserCard.tsx`, `useAuth.ts`)
    - Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE
  imports:
    - Group by: React → Next.js → Libraries → Local
    - Use absolute imports (`@/components/...`)
  commits:
    - Follow Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `refactor:`, etc.)
  testing:
    - Write testable components; consider adding Jest or Playwright later.
  responsiveness:
    - Always check Tailwind breakpoints (`sm`, `md`, `lg`, `xl`).
    - Use flex or grid for adaptive layouts.
    - Prefer relative units (%, rem, vw/vh) over px when possible.

folder_structure_example:
  app/
    layout.tsx        # Root layout
    page.tsx          # Home page
    dashboard/
      layout.tsx
      page.tsx
      settings/
        page.tsx
  components/
    ui/
      Button.tsx
      Card.tsx
    navigation/
      Navbar.tsx
      Sidebar.tsx
  lib/
    supabaseClient.ts
    utils.ts
  styles/
    globals.css
    tailwind.config.js
  hooks/
    useAuth.ts
    useTheme.ts
  types/
    user.ts
  context/
    AuthContext.tsx

quality:
  - All new files must pass TypeScript checks and ESLint rules.
  - No unused imports, variables, or commented-out code.
  - Keep functions under 100 lines.
  - Use async/await, avoid promise chaining.
  - Each PR must be reviewed for readability and reusability.

ai_guidelines:
  - When generating components, include type definitions and prop interfaces.
  - Use descriptive names and doc comments.
  - When generating Supabase queries, ensure proper error handling and typing.
  - Avoid redundant imports and ensure consistent code formatting (Prettier).
  - Generate Tailwind classes with readability and responsiveness in mind.
  - Generate layout code following Next.js official recommendations:
    https://nextjs.org/docs/pages/building-your-application/routing/pages-and-layouts
  - A PAGE MUST BE ALWAYS SERVERSIDE RENDERING, ONLY USED "use client" on a components